In d60.py, make an SSE endpoint with only the standard library's `http.server`: write `class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` with a `do_GET(self)` method, which the server calls for each GET request. In it, call `self.send_response(200)`, `self.send_header("Content-Type", "text/event-stream")` and `self.end_headers()` (which finishes the headers). Then, for n in 1 to 5, write `self.wfile.write(f"id: {n}
data: over {n}: 6 runs

".encode())` (wfile takes bytes, hence `.encode()`), call `self.wfile.flush()` and `time.sleep(1)`. At the bottom, `ThreadingHTTPServer(("localhost", 8060), Handler).serve_forever()`. Run it, and in another terminal run `curl -N localhost:8060`: the five events appear one per second, all on one response.
